  },
  "linkRules": {
    "_principle": "Links are resolved ROUTE-relative: every page route is its own directory, so one '..' pops exactly one path segment. fs.existsSync on the joined path is NOT a valid check - wrong-level links exist as files.",
    "leafToSibling": "../<Name>",
    "leafToCrossBucket": "../../<other-bucket>/<Name>",
    "leafToSectionIndex": "../",
    "bucketIndexToLeaf": "./<Name>",
    "bucketIndexToParentIndex": "../",
    "bucketIndexToLangRoot": "../../",
    "apiIndexToLangRoot": "../",
    "architectureToApiLeaf": "../../api/<bucket>/<Name>",
    "forbidden": [
      "content/ anywhere in an href - repo-root-relative leakage",
      "a version segment inside a SAME-version link",
      "../<bucket>/<Name> from a leaf page - one level short, only reachable as a sibling",
      "./<Name> from a leaf page - dot-slash is legal only from a bucket _index.md"
    ],
    "evidence": "shipped v1.4.5 zh/api uses 2+ '../' for 5215 cross-bucket links; the generated 1.4.7 tree emitted only 40 such links and 4135 one-'../' links carrying a bucket name, which is the defect signature",
    "gate": "For every emitted relative link: route(from) = the page's own route ending in '/'; target = normalize(route(from) + href) popping one segment per '..' and dropping '.'; assert exists(content/<target>.md) || exists(content/<target>/_index.md). PLUS a complementary reverse assertion on forbidden substrings - depth-only checks cannot see a wrong prefix, and a fix that satisfies the check which caught the previous bug can satisfy it while introducing a different bug.",
    "popToSiteRoot": "pops-to-site-root == number of segments in the page's OWN route. A leaf route v1.4.7/zh/architecture/version-delta/ has 4 segments and needs FOUR '../'; a section-index route v1.4.7/zh/architecture/ has 3 and needs THREE. Same-version links never need this (they stay inside the tree); cross-version links climb to the site root and therefore need the full pop count.",
    "crossVersion": "../ x(popToSiteRoot) / <version> / <lang> / <section> / <Name>. The language segment must match the TARGET tree, not the source. Verified correct: leaf -> ../../../../v1.4.5/zh/architecture/ ; index -> ../../../v1.4.5/zh/architecture/",
    "allowed": [
      "../<Name> (leaf -> same-bucket sibling)",
      "../../<other-bucket>/<Name> (leaf -> cross-bucket)",
      "../ (leaf or bucket index -> section index)",
      "./<Name> (bucket _index.md -> its leaf)",
      "cross-version: ('../' x popToSiteRoot) + <version>/<lang>/<section>/<Name>"
    ],
    "_forbiddenNote": "Refined from a blanket rule after lead-2 proved it wrong: 'no v1. in any href' would ban the ONLY correct form of a cross-version link, and would have flagged 6 genuinely-broken links as rule-compliant while leaving them broken. It mistakes the symptom for the disease. A cross-version href legitimately contains a version segment; what is forbidden is a version segment inside a SAME-version link."
  },
  "resolutionOrder": [
    "1. excludeNamespaces / excludeSuffixes / sourceTypoNamespaces  -> hard skip, no page, counted separately",
    "2. rules[] -> longest-prefix-wins. Record the matched rule (dirRule) but DO NOT return early.",
    "3. entryPointDirs -> override by exact case-sensitive simple type name. This step runs for EVERY type, including those whose namespace already matched a prefix rule in step 2. If no override matches, keep the step-2 result.",
    "4. defaultDir (core-extra) if step 2 matched nothing AND step 3 has no entry -> also record in unmapped"
  ],
  "parityGaps": [
    {
      "id": "no-gameplay-bucket",
      "from": "1.4.5/gameplay/",
      "to": "(none)",
      "pages": 19,
      "reason": "The 1.4.5 gameplay/ bucket is semantically mixed: it holds SandBox(4), StoryMode.*(4) and bare TaleWorlds.MountAndBlade types (AgentNavigator, MapAudioManager, OppositionData, DelayedAction, NameplateSize, ...). No namespace rule can reproduce it. Bucket deliberately NOT created - SandBox* -> sandbox and StoryMode* -> storymode, which match the real namespaces.",
      "decision": "accept the 19-URL break; do not invent a bucket to make numbers line up"
    },
    {
      "id": "mission-bulk-to-mission-ext",
      "from": "1.4.5/mission/",
      "to": "mission-ext/",
      "pages": 52,
      "reason": "52 of 1.4.5's 78 mission/ pages are bare TaleWorlds.MountAndBlade types (Agent, Formation, ActionIndexCache, AutoGeneratedSaveManager, BannerTextureCreator, AgentHelper, GenericMissionObjective, ...). That is a hand-picked modder entry list no namespace rule can reproduce; faking parity would mean shredding the ~850-page mission-ext bucket and hand-maintaining a list.",
      "decision": "accept; mission/ stays a small intentional entry-class carve-out with bidirectional links to ../mission-ext/"
    },
    {
      "id": "game-to-core-extra",
      "from": "1.4.5/core/Game.md",
      "to": "core-extra/Game.md",
      "pages": 1,
      "reason": "Game is namespace TaleWorlds.Core, which the prefix rules route to core-extra. 1.4.5 happens to keep a copy in core/ (and a duplicate in core-extra/).",
      "decision": "accept the 1-URL move; namespace consistency beats copying a legacy duplicate"
    },
    {
      "id": "missionstate-to-mission",
      "from": "1.4.5 mission-ext/MissionState.md (+ campaign-ext duplicate)",
      "to": "mission/MissionState.md",
      "pages": 1,
      "reason": "1.4.5 has MissionState duplicated in campaign-ext/ and mission-ext/ and no mission/ copy. The entryPointDirs carve-out groups it with Mission/Agent/Formation for modders.",
      "decision": "accept the 1-URL break for modder-facing grouping"
    },
    {
      "id": "boardgames-bucket-removed",
      "from": "1.4.5/boardgames/",
      "to": "sandbox/",
      "pages": 2,
      "reason": "1.5.3 has no TaleWorlds.BoardGames namespace (grep 0 hits); the 43 board-game types live in SandBox.BoardGames* child namespaces, which the SandBox -> sandbox rule already routes to sandbox/.",
      "decision": "do not create an empty bucket; a rule that can never match plus a permanently empty bucket is exactly the silent failure the non-empty assertion exists to catch"
    }
  ],
  "invariants": {
    "oneTypeOnePath": "A type has exactly one .md file. Same-directory collisions use <NamespaceLeaf>__<TypeName>.md. The 1.4.5 tree had 2,199 duplicated type names and 171 of 513 namespaces split across buckets.",
    "everyDirectoryHasIndex": "Every directory under content/v1.4.7/** contains an _index.md. Without it Zola does not build page.ancestors, so templates/macros/breadcrumb.html:10 stops early and the reader cannot walk back up.",
    "zhEnParity": "The zh and en trees have identical directory sets and identical _index.md sets. 1.4.5 violates this (zh/api/gameplay has 18 pages, en/api/gameplay does not exist).",
    "popToSiteRoot": "pops-to-site-root == the number of segments in the page own route. Same-version links never need it; cross-version links must climb to the site root and therefore carry the full pop count plus <version>/<lang>/<section>.",
    "forbidden": [
      "content/ anywhere in an href - repo-root-relative leakage",
      "a version segment inside a SAME-version link",
      "../<bucket>/<Name> from a leaf page - one level short, only reachable as a sibling",
      "./<Name> from a leaf page - dot-slash is legal only from a bucket _index.md"
    ],
    "landingDistance": "No route more than 3 levels below /v1.4.7/{lang}/ — tools/audit-navigation.mjs checkLandingDistance(expected, errors, 3).",
    "routeCountZeroOrphan": "Every route in data/navigation.json must correspond to a file on disk, else tools/audit-navigation.mjs reports \"navigation route is not a content section\"."
  },
  "noModuleManager": "There is NO ModuleManager type in any version (artifact entryPointDirs._noModuleManager). No such page or route exists or is specified.",
  "bucketsNotCreated": [
    "gameplay",
    "navigationsystem",
    "boardgames",
    "screensystem",
    "view",
    "perks",
    "final"
  ],
  "notCreatedReason": "gameplay and navigationsystem are ruled out by the Lead (parity gaps no-gameplay-bucket, and TaleWorlds.NavigationSystem -> core-extra). boardgames projects zero types (no TaleWorlds.BoardGames namespace). screensystem was reversed to gui. view/perks/final are 1.4.5-only shells with no canonical rule.",
  "bidirectionalLadder": {
    "_principle": "This is the acceptance criterion for \"the site sends me somewhere unrelated and I cannot get back\".",
    "hops": [
      {
        "step": 1,
        "from": "leaf  api/<bucket>/<Type>.md",
        "to": "same-directory index  api/<bucket>/",
        "link": "../",
        "route": "/v1.4.7/{lang}/api/<bucket>/",
        "renderNote": "templates/macros/page-navigation.html:29-30 renders this as the Parent link on every leaf"
      },
      {
        "step": 2,
        "from": "bucket index  api/<bucket>/_index.md",
        "to": "API hub  api/_index.md",
        "link": "../",
        "route": "/v1.4.7/{lang}/api/"
      },
      {
        "step": 3,
        "from": "API hub  api/_index.md",
        "to": "language home  _index.md",
        "link": "../",
        "route": "/v1.4.7/{lang}/"
      },
      {
        "step": 4,
        "from": "language home  _index.md",
        "to": "site home  content/_index.md",
        "link": "../../",
        "route": "/"
      },
      {
        "step": 5,
        "from": "site home",
        "to": "any version or section",
        "link": "./v1.4.7/{lang}/",
        "route": "/v1.4.7/{lang}/"
      }
    ],
    "siblingMovement": {
      "insideBucket": "Every bucket _index.md lists every one of its leaf pages, so sideways movement inside a bucket is one click.",
      "acrossBuckets": "Every bucket _index.md links to all 18 sibling bucket indexes via ../<bucket>/. The two carve-out buckets mission/ and core/ additionally state, in their first paragraph, that the bulk surface is in ../mission-ext/ and ../core-extra/, and mission-ext/_index.md and core-extra/_index.md point back.",
      "atRuntime": "templates/macros/page-navigation.html:33-42 renders prev/next for the adjacent leaves in the same directory; :45-53 renders a Related row from nav.routes[parent].children.",
      "upChain": "templates/macros/breadcrumb.html renders root -> every ancestor section -> current title, driven by Zola page.ancestors. This only works if every directory has an _index.md."
    }
  },
